---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import Solids from '@/components/tools/calc2/Solids.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="surface-area-calculator">
  <Solids client:load measure="surface" />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the surface area calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      The surface area calculator adds up the area of every face of the shape. It lists each part (bases,
      sides, the curved surface) and shows the shape unfolding into its net.
    </p>
    <pre><code>cube                A = 6a²
box                 A = 2(lw + lh + wh)
cylinder            A = 2πr² + 2πrh
cone                A = πr² + πrs,  s = √(r² + h²)
sphere              A = 4πr²
hemisphere          A = 3πr²   (curved 2πr² + flat πr²)
square pyramid      A = a² + 2as,   s = √((a ÷ 2)² + h²)
triangular prism    A = 2T + (a + b + c) × length</code></pre>

    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      A cylinder with a radius of 3 cm and a height of 5 cm has two circular ends of π × 3² = 28.274 cm²
      each and a curved side that unrolls into a rectangle of 2π × 3 × 5 = 94.248 cm². The total is
      150.796 cm².
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      A sphere has no flat net; its area equals four circles of the same radius, and the animation shows
      those. The results are for ideal shapes; for paint or wrapping, add 10 to 15% for overlaps and waste.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
